If a clinician starts an ER-LA-opioid for a patient then the clinician should consider a lower-end-follow-up-interval for the patient.
If a clinician increases an ER-LA-opioid-dosage for a patient then the clinician should consider a lower-end-follow-up-interval for the patient.
If a patient has a combined-opioid-dosage and the combined-opioid-dosage includes at least 50 MME-units-per-day then every clinician should consider a lower-end-follow-up-interval for the patient.
